{"agent":"fleet-smallcli","data":{"fix_task":"fix-Bf965d87b66","item":"","scope":"ddflow","severity":"medium","summary":"Observed 2026-10-16 in worktree fix-decision-extends-drops-globs while load average was ~550: 'git merge main' took 22m because the post-merge hook ran 'ddflow pins regenerate --after-merge' (which ran pytest tests/golden --snapshot-update serially), and after it finished 'git status' showed 'MM README.md' (git diff --stat: README.md 6473 lines changed, +6472) and ' D' for tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_mcp_tools.ambr, test_golden_outputs.ambr, test_uc_surf_reporting_pin.ambr (and test_golden_search.ambr emptied by 355 lines), plus tests/test_uc_surf_setup_ops_transcript.py failing. A second manual 'ddflow pins regenerate' printed 'golden-snapshots: re-recorded' and left the tree with README alone damaged; after 'git checkout HEAD -- README.md' a third 'ddflow pins regenerate' reported all pins current and the tree was clean. So a regeneration that overlaps with other work (or is interrupted by load/timeouts) is not atomic: it must write each pin to a temp file and rename, and refuse to leave a tree where README grows past its generator's output. Expected: the after-merge hook is idempotent and never leaves a damaged working tree.","title":"post-merge pins regenerate under heavy load leaves README with 6472 duplicated lines and deletes golden snapshots"},"id":"e123fcfcfc7bc54c4858483d9","kind":"bug.found","lamport":70865,"schema":1,"subject":"Bf965d87b66","ts":"2026-10-16T20:26:17.491686Z"}
{"agent":"fleet-smallcli","data":{"body":"Fixes bug Bf965d87b66: Observed 2026-10-16 in worktree fix-decision-extends-drops-globs while load average was ~550: 'git merge main' took 22m because the post-merge hook ran 'ddflow pins regenerate --after-merge' (which ran pytest tests/golden --snapshot-update serially), and after it finished 'git status' showed 'MM README.md' (git diff --stat: README.md 6473 lines changed, +6472) and ' D' for tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_mcp_tools.ambr, test_golden_outputs.ambr, test_uc_surf_reporting_pin.ambr (and test_golden_search.ambr emptied by 355 lines), plus tests/test_uc_surf_setup_ops_transcript.py failing. A second manual 'ddflow pins regenerate' printed 'golden-snapshots: re-recorded' and left the tree with README alone damaged; after 'git checkout HEAD -- README.md' a third 'ddflow pins regenerate' reported all pins current and the tree was clean. So a regeneration that overlaps with other work (or is interrupted by load/timeouts) is not atomic: it must write each pin to a temp file and rename, and refuse to leave a tree where README grows past its generator's output. Expected: the after-merge hook is idempotent and never leaves a damaged working tree.\n\nWrite the regression test first and watch it FAIL on the unfixed code; then `ddflow complete fix-Bf965d87b66 --regression-test <test>` closes the bug with the task (or `ddflow bug fixed Bf965d87b66 --regression-test <test>` first).","fixes":["Bf965d87b66"],"globs":["scripts/pins.py"],"line":"","needs":[],"parent":"","priority":100,"tags":["bugfix"],"title":"Fix bug Bf965d87b66: post-merge pins regenerate under heavy load leaves README with 6472 duplicated lines and deletes..."},"id":"e48bf1c1b93e421b3f910ad1d","kind":"task.added","lamport":70866,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-Bf965d87b66","ts":"2026-10-16T20:26:17.517192Z"}
